WEBVTT

00:00:15.340 --> 00:00:20.780
Miss. You were finally able to head off to Animal Village and we've run into rain.

00:00:20.780 --> 00:00:22.950
I like rainy days.

00:00:22.950 --> 00:00:28.920
With my favorite umbrella, I put on my boots
and splash around in the puddles.

00:00:29.420 --> 00:00:32.260
Well, all that matters is how you feel about it.

00:00:32.930 --> 00:00:39.150
Moving to that shabby village all by yourself; you must be self-reliant, Miss.

00:00:39.150 --> 00:00:41.850
No need to call me Miss, it's Ai.

00:00:41.850 --> 00:00:43.100
A,I,U,E,O, Ai.

00:00:43.100 --> 00:00:47.400
Ai-pe, is it? That's a nice name.

00:00:48.040 --> 00:00:49.820
Ai-pe?

00:01:15.620 --> 00:01:19.260
That spot where you see the rainbow
end is Animal Village.

00:01:19.760 --> 00:01:20.970
Over there is...

00:01:21.480 --> 00:01:22.720
Animal Village!

00:01:32.230 --> 00:01:34.860
Animal Crossing

00:01:34.860 --> 00:01:41.740
<b>Animal Crossing</b>
The Movie<b></b>

00:02:22.640 --> 00:02:24.040
Here's the town hall.

00:02:30.880 --> 00:02:32.620
Hi Animal Village!

00:02:32.620 --> 00:02:34.040
My name is Ai!

00:02:34.040 --> 00:02:36.510
I've moved to the village today!

00:02:43.260 --> 00:02:45.700
Don't worry, I can handle this.

00:02:45.700 --> 00:02:47.100
Really?

00:02:53.730 --> 00:02:56.060
Indeed, you prefer to be self-reliant.

00:03:12.870 --> 00:03:16.460
You must be Miss Ai, right? The one who is moving here.

00:03:17.440 --> 00:03:19.510
Yes, pleased to meet you.

00:03:19.510 --> 00:03:21.660
My name is Peliko.

00:03:22.130 --> 00:03:26.520
Ever since you contacted us, I've been getting everything ready.

00:03:26.900 --> 00:03:31.350
If you need any help or don't understand something, feel free to ask me, 'kay?

00:03:32.150 --> 00:03:34.270
I'll always be here in the daytime.

00:03:35.190 --> 00:03:36.190
Okay.

00:03:36.550 --> 00:03:39.630
At night is my older sister, so you can visit too.

00:03:40.300 --> 00:03:43.610
Staying open 24 hours, that's so modern.

00:03:50.040 --> 00:03:53.970
You must be our new resident
Miss Ai, am I right?

00:03:53.970 --> 00:03:54.520
Yes!

00:03:54.520 --> 00:03:56.720
I'm Kotobuki the mayor.

00:03:57.360 --> 00:04:00.630
Let me help you remember, I'm Kotobuki the mayor.

00:04:01.110 --> 00:04:01.780
Yes.

00:04:01.780 --> 00:04:05.220
I know this is sudden, but may I ask you a question?

00:04:05.220 --> 00:04:06.190
A question?

00:04:06.190 --> 00:04:10.680
In the up-coming ballots, Who do you think is most qualified.

00:04:12.390 --> 00:04:13.980
1 Me, the mayor.

00:04:13.980 --> 00:04:15.900
2 Me, the mayor.

00:04:15.900 --> 00:04:17.820
3 Me, the mayor.

00:04:17.820 --> 00:04:20.080
4 Me, the mayor.

00:04:20.080 --> 00:04:22.090
They're all the mayor?

00:04:22.090 --> 00:04:25.160
That was a pretty cold-hearted remark.

00:04:25.160 --> 00:04:27.490
Please reply to Mr. Mayor's question.

00:04:28.490 --> 00:04:33.080
This winter we'll be having another election.

00:04:33.550 --> 00:04:37.710
Mayor Kotobuki is always worrying about it.

00:04:37.710 --> 00:04:40.000
Election? For the mayor?

00:04:42.160 --> 00:04:44.940
The mayor! Yes, the mayor.

00:04:45.460 --> 00:04:49.390
Mayor number... any number you want.

00:04:50.000 --> 00:04:51.730
I see! I see!

00:04:52.310 --> 00:04:57.830
I am really touched to have Miss Ai supporting me within the Animal Village.

00:05:00.140 --> 00:05:03.370
Miss Ai, your landlord will be Mr. Tanukichi.

00:05:03.370 --> 00:05:07.480
Please head to Tanuki Goods shop and pick up the key.

00:05:07.800 --> 00:05:11.240
(Tanuki Goods)

00:05:16.010 --> 00:05:17.120
Welcome!

00:05:17.120 --> 00:05:20.480
Come in, come in! Please feel
free to browse around.

00:05:20.480 --> 00:05:22.730
What in particular were you searching for?

00:05:22.730 --> 00:05:26.420
Well, no, I didn't come here to buy something.

00:05:26.420 --> 00:05:27.870
My name is Ai.

00:05:27.870 --> 00:05:32.020
I was told by Miss Peliko to come find Mr. Tanukichi who will be my landlord.

00:05:32.910 --> 00:05:37.300
Is that right? You should've mentioned that from the start.

00:05:37.690 --> 00:05:38.820
I'm sorry.

00:05:38.820 --> 00:05:40.530
Okay, put this on.

00:05:42.920 --> 00:05:45.860
I need you to start working right away.

00:05:45.860 --> 00:05:46.900
Work?

00:05:50.280 --> 00:05:53.080
Okay, take care of the deliveries.

00:05:53.080 --> 00:05:54.370
Deliveries?

00:05:54.630 --> 00:05:58.910
I just came to get a key, I wasn't really looking for work.

00:05:58.910 --> 00:06:03.670
The quickest way for you to get used to your new life in Animal Village is by working.

00:06:04.510 --> 00:06:05.880
Is that true?

00:06:05.880 --> 00:06:07.210
How's that?

00:06:07.210 --> 00:06:11.350
While working you can introduce yourself to all the residents, it's two birds with one stone.

00:06:11.350 --> 00:06:13.260
Well, that might be true.

00:06:13.260 --> 00:06:16.180
It's not, "Well, that might be true," it's yes, that is true.

00:06:16.180 --> 00:06:18.350
But still, it's so sudden.

00:06:18.350 --> 00:06:21.470
Come now, come now. Time is money they say.

00:06:23.880 --> 00:06:25.070
Oh well, sure.

00:06:25.070 --> 00:06:27.280
Here is the delivery list.

00:06:27.280 --> 00:06:28.360
Okay!

00:06:28.970 --> 00:06:31.280
Well, I'm off!

00:06:35.200 --> 00:06:40.630
There's still a lot left to be delivered so I want you to come back right away!

00:06:44.740 --> 00:06:47.140
An uphill challenge.

00:07:18.450 --> 00:07:21.620
Let's see, this one.

00:07:27.540 --> 00:07:31.010
Miss Bouquet, I have a delivery from Tanuki Goods.

00:07:33.500 --> 00:07:35.770
Finally, it's here!

00:07:35.770 --> 00:07:37.770
Excuse me, from today onward...

00:07:38.360 --> 00:07:39.770
How is it? How is it?

00:07:40.200 --> 00:07:41.560
It looks real good.

00:07:41.560 --> 00:07:45.780
You see, today I came to the Animal Village.

00:07:46.160 --> 00:07:48.870
I must really be dynamite.

00:07:49.240 --> 00:07:53.550
Everything I put on looks so cute, amazing!

00:07:53.550 --> 00:07:54.320
Excuse me.

00:07:54.640 --> 00:07:56.330
Hey, you're a newcomer right?

00:07:57.490 --> 00:07:59.210
Why did you move here?

00:07:59.210 --> 00:07:59.720
Alone?

00:07:59.720 --> 00:08:02.030
Or are you living with a friend?

00:08:02.030 --> 00:08:03.450
Or how about, how about...

00:08:03.450 --> 00:08:04.460
I'm alone.

00:08:04.800 --> 00:08:07.090
Alone is it?

00:08:07.680 --> 00:08:08.770
I got it!

00:08:08.770 --> 00:08:12.050
You are running away from your former home.

00:08:12.050 --> 00:08:14.760
In order to forget him and to heal your broken heart,

00:08:14.760 --> 00:08:16.980
you have naturally set off on a solitary journey.

00:08:17.380 --> 00:08:22.070
And finally, you have arrived at this far-off village!

00:08:22.070 --> 00:08:22.940
That's not it.

00:08:23.490 --> 00:08:24.650
It has to be.

00:08:25.730 --> 00:08:30.170
I also want to be taken away by my prince on a white horse!

00:08:35.570 --> 00:08:38.370
Mr. Halberd, I have a delivery.

00:08:39.640 --> 00:08:42.640
Thank you for leaving the delivery of five hundred pies to...

00:08:43.050 --> 00:08:44.290
Five hundred pies?!

00:08:46.790 --> 00:08:48.340
You see, today is...

00:08:49.380 --> 00:08:50.840
It's here, it's here!

00:08:51.760 --> 00:08:55.140
Just remembering the taste by indulging in the smell coming from this box.

00:08:55.140 --> 00:08:58.260
It's like I'm about to be enchanted into a dream.

00:08:58.260 --> 00:08:59.430
Excuse me...

00:08:59.770 --> 00:09:03.420
Hey you, custard or tiramisu, which do you prefer?

00:09:03.830 --> 00:09:07.050
As for me, I like them both!

00:09:09.860 --> 00:09:10.570
Who's that?

00:09:10.570 --> 00:09:11.900
Wait!

00:09:11.900 --> 00:09:14.570
Wait up!

00:09:15.640 --> 00:09:16.790
Ninja?

00:09:16.790 --> 00:09:17.960
Why's there...?

00:09:19.540 --> 00:09:21.490
What'll I do, he left?

00:09:23.500 --> 00:09:24.410
It can't be helped.

00:09:28.190 --> 00:09:31.560
I'm the one supposed to be moving, what's going on here.

00:09:35.110 --> 00:09:38.880
Excuse me, Miss Bianca, I'm from Tanuki Goods.

00:09:38.880 --> 00:09:40.260
I have a delivery.

00:09:40.260 --> 00:09:40.890
Thank you.

00:09:41.650 --> 00:09:44.170
It's open so may I please ask you to leave it inside?

00:09:44.170 --> 00:09:45.030
Yes.

00:09:47.060 --> 00:09:48.480
You just started, right?

00:09:49.120 --> 00:09:49.900
Yes!

00:09:50.180 --> 00:09:53.320
You have that glimmering sparkle
in every sense. It's lovely, yes?

00:09:54.560 --> 00:09:58.250
Well, delivery work might be lacking romance and might be quite laborious,

00:09:58.710 --> 00:10:01.460
but a polished lady will shine brightly in any circumstance.

00:10:01.910 --> 00:10:02.610
Yes.

00:10:02.960 --> 00:10:07.410
Whenever you need, come see me and I'll help you learn to be a lady in any situation, yes?

00:10:17.570 --> 00:10:19.590
She was a beautiful person.

00:10:27.610 --> 00:10:28.640
Welcome!

00:10:29.000 --> 00:10:32.570
I'm from Tanuki Goods. I'm here to deliver your order.

00:10:32.870 --> 00:10:35.650
Thank you for the hard work. Please leave it in that area.

00:10:36.020 --> 00:10:36.710
Yes.

00:10:41.000 --> 00:10:42.550
Cute clothes!

00:10:47.920 --> 00:10:48.910
Good afternoon.

00:10:49.700 --> 00:10:51.010
Hey there, Sally!

00:10:51.010 --> 00:10:51.830
Welcome.

00:10:56.770 --> 00:10:59.220
I'm sorry to always bother you during work.

00:10:59.220 --> 00:11:04.260
It's fine, today we get to see another one of Sally's designs, right?

00:11:04.260 --> 00:11:08.650
Yes, I'm always excited to see another one of Sally's wonderful designs.

00:11:08.650 --> 00:11:09.270
Excuse me.
Yes, I'm always excited to see another one of Sally's wonderful designs.

00:11:09.270 --> 00:11:09.600
Excuse me.

00:11:09.600 --> 00:11:11.260
Come now, show it to us.

00:11:17.320 --> 00:11:19.240
(Tanuki Goods)

00:11:19.620 --> 00:11:22.850
I'll be waiting for you tomorrow!

00:11:36.760 --> 00:11:39.020
That was a long first day.

00:11:48.650 --> 00:11:49.680
That's it, there.

00:11:52.720 --> 00:11:53.650
Let's go!

00:11:54.820 --> 00:11:58.820
In that house will be the commencement of my first time alone.

00:12:08.690 --> 00:12:09.760
Don't move!

00:12:09.760 --> 00:12:12.000
The spider will get away!

00:12:14.500 --> 00:12:16.370
That's why I said don't move!

00:12:18.380 --> 00:12:20.340
Wait!

00:12:21.760 --> 00:12:25.330
All right! I finally caught the rare spider!

00:12:25.330 --> 00:12:34.230
I beat Halberd!

00:12:34.860 --> 00:12:36.590
Wait now! What do you think..!

00:12:36.590 --> 00:12:37.150
Huh?

00:12:37.150 --> 00:12:39.570
You're that afternoon ninja.

00:12:41.390 --> 00:12:42.010
For you.

00:12:43.160 --> 00:12:45.250
I'm Yu from the nearby village.

00:12:45.250 --> 00:12:47.280
I often come here to play.

00:12:49.980 --> 00:12:53.550
That's not exactly how this conversation was supposed to continue.

00:12:53.550 --> 00:12:55.370
Anyway, I was able to catch the spider.

00:12:56.050 --> 00:12:57.660
And it was the two of us.

00:12:57.660 --> 00:12:59.130
Two of us?

00:12:59.800 --> 00:13:00.570
For you.

00:14:06.540 --> 00:14:09.320
Mr. Apollo, I have a delivery.

00:14:13.870 --> 00:14:15.130
Mr. Apollo?

00:14:21.680 --> 00:14:22.660
Wait!

00:14:22.660 --> 00:14:25.110
Wait, wait!

00:14:36.050 --> 00:14:36.980
Him again!

00:14:37.980 --> 00:14:39.650
HEY YOU!

00:14:41.120 --> 00:14:43.290
You there, what did you do!

00:14:44.130 --> 00:14:47.560
Oh? Now that I look closer I've never seen your face before.

00:14:48.150 --> 00:14:49.110
You're a new resident?

00:14:50.890 --> 00:14:51.950
And, your name is?

00:14:52.820 --> 00:14:54.540
It's... Ai.

00:14:54.780 --> 00:14:55.980
Ai, is it?

00:14:55.980 --> 00:14:58.560
Well, since you're new, it can't be helped.

00:14:59.720 --> 00:15:02.630
DON'T THINK I'LL GO TOO EASY ON YOU!

00:15:04.600 --> 00:15:07.010
Reactions determine people's true character.

00:15:07.730 --> 00:15:11.550
Since you're new, you probably don't know about me, so here's my introduction.

00:15:12.390 --> 00:15:18.560
I am the enforcer of justice towards people who break the rules in Animal Village, Mr. Reset.

00:15:18.560 --> 00:15:19.980
Pleased to meet'cha.

00:15:20.840 --> 00:15:21.900
Likewise.

00:15:22.210 --> 00:15:24.810
Now the problem is this garden, right?

00:15:27.620 --> 00:15:29.050
I'm sorry!

00:15:29.700 --> 00:15:31.230
What should I do about this?

00:15:31.790 --> 00:15:33.820
Well, by the looks of it...

00:15:34.240 --> 00:15:36.740
You didn't do it on purpose.

00:15:37.060 --> 00:15:39.440
No need for a lecture then.

00:15:40.080 --> 00:15:43.830
But of all the gardens, it had to be Apollo's garden, right?

00:15:43.830 --> 00:15:46.150
You must be real unlucky.

00:15:46.150 --> 00:15:46.950
See you!

00:15:48.100 --> 00:15:53.470
Mr. Reset! Apollo is not home, do you know where he could be?

00:15:53.470 --> 00:15:55.400
How 'bout checking the Pigeon's Roost?

00:15:55.400 --> 00:15:58.250
Apollo visits that place quite often.

00:16:02.540 --> 00:16:03.710
Good after-?

00:16:24.970 --> 00:16:25.510
Fuko?

00:16:25.510 --> 00:16:26.460
Futo!

00:16:27.220 --> 00:16:28.820
Did you hear that just now?

00:16:28.820 --> 00:16:31.170
Yes, it came from that direction.

00:16:40.490 --> 00:16:42.810
Excuse me, are you okay?

00:16:45.610 --> 00:16:47.460
The person screaming, was it you?

00:16:49.400 --> 00:16:50.550
I'm sorry.

00:16:50.550 --> 00:16:52.780
The door was open and I came in and got surprised.

00:16:54.160 --> 00:16:55.320
Um, this place is?

00:16:56.950 --> 00:16:58.840
Wonderful!

00:17:11.160 --> 00:17:12.620
T-Rex.

00:17:12.620 --> 00:17:14.700
Approximately 43 feet in length.

00:17:14.700 --> 00:17:16.180
Existing during the Cretaceous Period.

00:17:16.180 --> 00:17:21.590
The T-Rex is the pinnacle of the -saurus, in particular, the most fearsome carnivore

00:17:21.590 --> 00:17:26.110
within the superfamily Tyrannosauroidea belonging to the genus Therapods.

00:17:26.110 --> 00:17:28.630
By the way, the terminology can be split into parts.

00:17:28.630 --> 00:17:32.820
Tyrannosaurus meaning "tyrant lizard" and Rex from the latin meaning "king".

00:17:33.620 --> 00:17:36.110
When my brother starts talking, he's never going to stop.

00:17:36.620 --> 00:17:38.730
Wasn't there are reason for your visit today?

00:17:39.130 --> 00:17:40.160
Let's see...

00:17:40.160 --> 00:17:43.670
I'm Ai. I just moved to the village.

00:17:44.080 --> 00:17:49.160
I have a delivery for Mr. Apollo and I heard he might be at the Pigeon's Roost, so...

00:17:49.160 --> 00:17:53.200
Is that right? Well then, let me show you the way. Over here.

00:17:59.890 --> 00:18:00.760
This is?

00:18:02.020 --> 00:18:05.360
That is the display case reserved for a Seismosaurus.

00:18:05.360 --> 00:18:06.690
Seismosaurus?

00:18:06.890 --> 00:18:07.880
Yes!

00:18:08.560 --> 00:18:10.960
It is said to be the largest of all animals.

00:18:10.960 --> 00:18:14.540
It's length could reach over 177 ft.

00:18:14.540 --> 00:18:17.460
The name means "Earth-shaking lizard".

00:18:17.460 --> 00:18:20.370
It is believed that it could eat up to 500 kg a day in plants.

00:18:20.370 --> 00:18:21.600
This way.
It is believed that it could eat up to 500 kg a day in plants.

00:18:21.600 --> 00:18:21.900
It is believed that it could eat up to 500 kg a day in plants.

00:18:23.010 --> 00:18:26.830
I can't wait for the day when we complete the Seismosaurus display.

00:18:29.730 --> 00:18:31.990
We have an observatory on the rooftop.

00:18:32.350 --> 00:18:33.570
On the roof?

00:18:33.570 --> 00:18:35.710
I always hang out there.

00:18:35.710 --> 00:18:39.350
So when you have some free time come and visit, 'kay?

00:18:39.350 --> 00:18:39.890
Yes!

00:18:40.040 --> 00:18:45.250
Animal Village is the best place for viewing stars. They are so pretty, you'll be surprised.

00:18:45.250 --> 00:18:47.060
Especially in the winter.

00:18:53.790 --> 00:18:56.820
Delicious coffee and wonderfully matched music.

00:18:57.450 --> 00:18:59.800
Coming here is always the best.

00:18:59.800 --> 00:19:02.050
The coffee is the best, but perhaps not the music?

00:19:02.050 --> 00:19:03.220
Excuse me.
The coffee is the best, but perhaps not the music?

00:19:03.220 --> 00:19:03.370
Excuse me.
What music would you prefer?

00:19:03.370 --> 00:19:05.200
What music would you prefer?
I'm searching for someone.

00:19:05.200 --> 00:19:05.710
What music would you prefer?

00:19:05.710 --> 00:19:08.960
Real men prefer enka, definitely enka.

00:19:08.960 --> 00:19:09.900
Here I go.
Real men prefer enka, definitely enka.

00:19:09.900 --> 00:19:10.630
Here I go.

00:19:14.950 --> 00:19:15.840
Excuse me.

00:19:16.580 --> 00:19:18.800
Mr. Apollo?

00:19:22.070 --> 00:19:25.690
I can't believe I would be mistaken for Apollo.

00:19:25.690 --> 00:19:28.230
We are definitely not as eccentric as him.

00:19:29.660 --> 00:19:30.890
Forgive me.

00:19:31.140 --> 00:19:35.830
But you know, Apollo used to be such a friendly person.

00:19:35.830 --> 00:19:39.070
Well, that was before he started to try and take off from the village.

00:19:44.990 --> 00:19:46.480
Coffee, same as usual.

00:19:46.870 --> 00:19:48.250
Right away.

00:19:48.250 --> 00:19:50.260
Speak of the devil.

00:19:51.450 --> 00:19:52.480
Please go ahead.

00:19:57.250 --> 00:19:59.140
Silent as usual.

00:19:59.140 --> 00:20:01.120
He seems to be in a foul mood.

00:20:01.120 --> 00:20:02.940
What's up, Apollo?

00:20:04.480 --> 00:20:07.180
Someone made a mess in my garden.

00:20:08.450 --> 00:20:10.510
After I finally got the blue roses to bloom.

00:20:17.540 --> 00:20:18.210
Excuse me.

00:20:19.640 --> 00:20:20.920
I have a delivery.

00:20:21.600 --> 00:20:23.000
Tanuki Goods is it?

00:20:25.300 --> 00:20:26.620
I'm sorry!

00:20:26.620 --> 00:20:28.790
I'm the person who messed up your garden!

00:20:31.240 --> 00:20:34.030
I came to deliver the goods, but you were out.

00:20:34.030 --> 00:20:36.130
Then a ninja appeared and...

00:20:36.130 --> 00:20:40.300
Anyway, I'm the one at fault for hurting the roses.

00:20:42.390 --> 00:20:43.930
I'm really sorry!

00:20:46.010 --> 00:20:48.090
Master, the coffee was superb.

00:21:05.710 --> 00:21:07.280
Another delivery right?

00:21:07.280 --> 00:21:08.660
Let me help.

00:21:08.660 --> 00:21:11.430
Thank you, but I can handle something like this.

00:21:14.500 --> 00:21:16.400
I have a lot of strength.

00:21:16.400 --> 00:21:19.080
That seems to be one of my talents.

00:21:19.630 --> 00:21:22.460
Since I finally have a chance to use it, it's more efficient.

00:21:23.720 --> 00:21:24.720
Efficient?

00:21:28.710 --> 00:21:30.420
Cherries!

00:21:31.750 --> 00:21:34.680
You can only get them in this village.

00:21:36.870 --> 00:21:40.180
Let's say we were creating cherry pies.

00:21:40.640 --> 00:21:43.610
But they are not triangle slices, they are circles!

00:21:46.030 --> 00:21:49.190
Let's ponder how we would eat them alone.

00:21:49.640 --> 00:21:52.170
Eating the first slice and second is no problem.

00:21:52.170 --> 00:21:56.920
But when I get to the third slice, my head is full of thoughts of dieting.

00:21:56.920 --> 00:21:58.540
Yes, yes! That often happens.

00:21:59.090 --> 00:22:01.420
When that happens, what do you do?

00:22:02.400 --> 00:22:08.390
I say to myself, I really shouldn't eat them, but then I stuff my face with them all.

00:22:08.390 --> 00:22:10.090
That's just like me.

00:22:10.090 --> 00:22:14.510
I mean, if you're not going to eat them, they will just be left in the refrigerator.

00:22:14.510 --> 00:22:18.940
As time passes, you forget about them, and it only leads to tragedy.

00:22:18.940 --> 00:22:20.480
Yes, yes.

00:22:21.760 --> 00:22:24.750
I believe thinking about things is also a talent.

00:22:24.750 --> 00:22:26.880
Only because it would be a waste not to eat the food.

00:22:27.240 --> 00:22:30.410
You have to keep using them, or your talents may become rusty.

00:22:31.380 --> 00:22:32.910
Keep using them?

00:22:33.060 --> 00:22:38.830
So you see, by helping you, I was also able to help myself.

00:22:46.040 --> 00:22:46.940
Here you go.

00:22:47.510 --> 00:22:48.540
Thank you.

00:22:53.460 --> 00:22:54.960
Delicious!

00:22:54.960 --> 00:22:56.660
I love cherries!

00:22:56.660 --> 00:22:58.150
Actually, me too!

00:23:00.320 --> 00:23:01.430
My name is Ai.

00:23:01.430 --> 00:23:02.650
A, I, U, E, O, Ai.

00:23:02.990 --> 00:23:04.820
My name is Sally.

00:23:14.310 --> 00:23:15.250
Mother.

00:23:15.780 --> 00:23:18.980
I seem to be getting used to life in Animal village.

00:23:20.440 --> 00:23:25.150
I'm starting to make acquaintances, and I have a friend named Sally.

00:23:26.580 --> 00:23:30.750
Today, we were planting cherry trees.

00:23:32.520 --> 00:23:33.950
That's great!

00:23:33.950 --> 00:23:36.350
Becoming a designer is my dream!

00:23:37.020 --> 00:23:43.020
I hope, one day, people all over the world will be able to wear my clothes.

00:23:43.020 --> 00:23:44.920
That's a grand dream.

00:23:45.490 --> 00:23:47.420
This sketch book is...

00:23:48.390 --> 00:23:50.280
Sally's cherry pie, right?

00:23:53.390 --> 00:23:54.010
Here.

00:23:56.200 --> 00:23:57.950
Just like you said.

00:23:59.000 --> 00:24:00.890
This is my cherry pie.

00:24:02.580 --> 00:24:07.090
Mother, since we'll be gathering a lot more cherries,

00:24:07.340 --> 00:24:09.740
please send me some more cherry pie recipes.

00:24:23.820 --> 00:24:25.300
A message bottle?

00:24:32.500 --> 00:24:34.430
"Above the pine forest,

00:24:34.430 --> 00:24:37.200
on the night of the winter festival, a miracle will occur."

00:24:38.270 --> 00:24:39.920
Pine forest?

00:24:40.560 --> 00:24:42.870
The night of the winter festival?

00:24:43.540 --> 00:24:44.930
A miracle?

00:24:48.930 --> 00:24:50.080
UFO?

00:24:52.160 --> 00:24:54.100
It can't be?

00:25:17.460 --> 00:25:19.740
Mayor, that's dangerous!

00:25:37.680 --> 00:25:41.380
Bianca always looks lovely!

00:25:42.230 --> 00:25:47.330
Do you know the rumor going around that Bianca and Apollo were a couple?

00:25:47.330 --> 00:25:48.010
What?

00:25:48.520 --> 00:25:50.380
You mean that  Apollo?

00:25:50.380 --> 00:25:53.940
Yep, the owner of the garden you messed up, Apollo.

00:25:54.120 --> 00:25:55.880
Don't remind me...

00:25:56.450 --> 00:26:00.870
It seems Apollo is still mad at me.

00:26:01.440 --> 00:26:06.290
I can't believe that grumpy old man and Bianca were a couple.

00:26:06.630 --> 00:26:09.750
Bouquet, don't spread rumors around too much.

00:26:11.500 --> 00:26:16.080
And what about you? Infatuated with that box, when are we going to swim?

00:26:16.430 --> 00:26:18.640
I'll be done in a 'sec.

00:26:18.640 --> 00:26:21.640
We haven't even taken a dip once today!

00:26:22.110 --> 00:26:28.930
Miss Asami said she would select one of my designs and help me find a store to carry it.

00:26:30.070 --> 00:26:32.160
So, I have to try hard.

00:26:34.900 --> 00:26:37.900
That's great. Sally has her own dream.

00:26:39.090 --> 00:26:46.200
I've thought it over many times, and I still don't know if I have what it takes.

00:26:46.710 --> 00:26:51.750
If someone asked, "Do you like doing this?" then I would have to say, "Yes, I like doing this."

00:26:52.910 --> 00:26:54.770
You do, for sure!

00:26:55.640 --> 00:26:58.460
Sally's drawings are all great.

00:26:58.460 --> 00:27:00.260
Put in lots of effort!

00:27:00.260 --> 00:27:03.850
And then, you gotta eat that special cherry pie you're making!

00:27:04.630 --> 00:27:05.390
Right?

00:27:09.580 --> 00:27:10.700
Cherry pie?

00:27:11.190 --> 00:27:12.360
All done!

00:27:45.440 --> 00:27:46.270
Found it?

00:27:46.270 --> 00:27:47.720
Nope.

00:27:52.730 --> 00:27:55.980
~Mr. fossil, come out and play!~

00:27:57.540 --> 00:27:59.230
Hey! I found something!

00:27:59.790 --> 00:28:00.810
Really?

00:28:04.580 --> 00:28:06.240
HEY YOU!

00:28:08.750 --> 00:28:12.740
Stop making so many holes all over the place!

00:28:13.430 --> 00:28:18.070
Thanks to you all my precious tunnels are starting to cave in!

00:28:18.070 --> 00:28:25.510
Kids being rambunctious digging holes all over my house, isn't that great!

00:28:26.200 --> 00:28:28.710
Don't tell me you did it on purpose?

00:28:29.710 --> 00:28:30.930
No, we didn't...

00:28:30.930 --> 00:28:32.440
Not at all.

00:28:32.870 --> 00:28:36.870
Of course you didn't! There would be no end to how sorry you would be if you did.

00:28:36.870 --> 00:28:39.780
Looking for fossils is fine, but there has to be a better method.

00:28:39.780 --> 00:28:41.410
Run away.
Looking for fossils is fine, but there has to be a better method.

00:28:42.220 --> 00:28:45.680
Listen, there are reasons for the rules in place.

00:28:45.680 --> 00:28:46.370
Run away.
Listen, there are reasons for the rules in place.

00:28:46.370 --> 00:28:47.220
Listen, there are reasons for the rules in place.
Run!

00:28:47.220 --> 00:28:47.510
Listen, there are reasons for the rules in place.

00:28:47.670 --> 00:28:48.620
HEY YOU!

00:28:48.790 --> 00:28:50.290
Mr. Reset, we're sorry!

00:28:50.290 --> 00:28:51.290
Sorry!

00:28:51.290 --> 00:28:52.960
RUNNING AWAY!

00:28:55.240 --> 00:28:57.380
Another tunnel caving in!

00:28:59.800 --> 00:29:01.230
(Tanuki Goods)

00:29:01.230 --> 00:29:03.170
All right!

00:29:03.580 --> 00:29:05.750
Sally's designs are almost ready.

00:29:05.750 --> 00:29:09.220
Let's definitely wear them to Totakeke's next live concert!

00:29:09.220 --> 00:29:10.780
You betcha'!

00:29:10.780 --> 00:29:11.740
Thank you.

00:29:16.320 --> 00:29:17.160
Ai.

00:29:17.160 --> 00:29:18.080
Bouquet.

00:29:30.030 --> 00:29:31.410
Another one showed up.

00:29:37.490 --> 00:29:40.130
"Plant pine trees as marked on the map,

00:29:42.930 --> 00:29:45.410
in order for the miracle during the winter festival."

00:29:45.410 --> 00:29:46.700
More?

00:30:03.900 --> 00:30:05.040
Miss Peliko!

00:30:05.040 --> 00:30:07.860
My, everyone's gathered!

00:30:08.250 --> 00:30:11.320
We are preparing for the fireworks festival.

00:30:11.320 --> 00:30:15.290
This year is special, we will have a stage setup.

00:30:15.520 --> 00:30:19.760
Before the fireworks, Totakeke is going to perform!

00:30:22.090 --> 00:30:25.830
I really want to hear K.K. Bossa!

00:30:25.830 --> 00:30:26.960
You find it?

00:30:26.960 --> 00:30:28.140
Nope.

00:30:28.550 --> 00:30:30.640
Just another haniwa.

00:30:37.180 --> 00:30:40.320
Another one of those crazy get-ups he's in.

00:30:40.320 --> 00:30:41.900
What're you guys doing?

00:30:43.620 --> 00:30:45.120
Hey you guys.

00:30:45.850 --> 00:30:46.820
Got it!

00:30:47.680 --> 00:30:50.220
Finally an ammonite fossil get!

00:30:50.760 --> 00:30:55.240
Just by a thread, now our collection is complete!

00:30:55.530 --> 00:30:58.600
~Found it! Found it! Found it! Hoi!~

00:30:58.600 --> 00:31:01.170
~Fossil of a fishy, found it! Hoi!~

00:31:01.550 --> 00:31:04.470
~An ammonite fossil it is! Hoi!~

00:31:04.870 --> 00:31:07.090
~Come on! Fossil it is! Hoi!~

00:31:07.650 --> 00:31:09.340
These boys...

00:31:09.340 --> 00:31:13.480
Being so happy over such a small thing.

00:31:13.480 --> 00:31:15.010
Makes me jealous.

00:31:15.280 --> 00:31:19.470
But you know, I've seen tons of those in the other place.

00:31:20.350 --> 00:31:21.280
For real?

00:31:21.280 --> 00:31:23.200
I want to go. Take us?

00:31:23.200 --> 00:31:26.780
Please! Let's go soon! Let's go fast! Let's go together!

00:31:26.780 --> 00:31:28.920
Right, right, right?

00:31:29.320 --> 00:31:30.960
I got it already!

00:31:31.510 --> 00:31:33.700
I'll take you so let go.

00:31:36.160 --> 00:31:37.620
How many...?

00:31:47.100 --> 00:31:50.340
You scalliwags, to the treasure! Forward Ho!

00:31:50.570 --> 00:31:52.370
Oh!

00:31:52.370 --> 00:31:53.580
Oh...

00:31:54.640 --> 00:31:57.660
Let's go! Into the cave of secrets!

00:31:57.660 --> 00:32:01.080
Into the cave of secrets!

00:32:01.080 --> 00:32:02.900
These boys...

00:32:12.880 --> 00:32:15.200
Such a cool place exists!

00:32:15.640 --> 00:32:17.540
I'm getting excited!

00:32:17.540 --> 00:32:20.630
Fossil sweetie, wait for me.

00:32:22.040 --> 00:32:23.280
A breeze?

00:32:23.280 --> 00:32:25.610
It's summer but in here its pretty cold.

00:32:25.610 --> 00:32:29.050
Bouquet, do they really have fossils in here?

00:32:29.490 --> 00:32:31.010
I think so...

00:32:31.300 --> 00:32:32.410
You think so?

00:32:32.410 --> 00:32:35.850
Actually, it was such a long time ago.

00:32:43.710 --> 00:32:45.840
Which path should we take?

00:32:45.840 --> 00:32:47.920
Answer me, swabby Bouquet.

00:32:48.370 --> 00:32:50.620
Who are you calling a swabby! But...

00:32:52.360 --> 00:32:53.130
Right!

00:32:53.130 --> 00:32:54.220
Right it is!

00:33:16.790 --> 00:33:17.680
What's that?

00:33:20.170 --> 00:33:21.070
Waterfall!

00:33:30.270 --> 00:33:32.490
Sorry, it was left!

00:33:32.490 --> 00:33:34.470
Too late now!

00:33:41.230 --> 00:33:44.510
Pushing forward is the only choice.

00:33:47.740 --> 00:33:48.250
Pardon me.

00:33:53.190 --> 00:33:58.330
Let's see now. Have I seen this resident in Animal village before?

00:34:06.240 --> 00:34:09.590
I can't, this is no time to space out.

00:34:10.240 --> 00:34:15.360
This is a great chance for me to use my leadership appeal.

00:34:16.070 --> 00:34:19.070
Sir, do I resemble anyone you know?

00:34:22.290 --> 00:34:25.490
Another villager who doesn't recognize me.

00:34:26.350 --> 00:34:30.460
My ratings must be at an all-time low.

00:34:30.840 --> 00:34:36.570
You shouldn't be surprised looking at a visitor.

00:34:37.030 --> 00:34:39.970
But you shouldn't look at them expecting too much neither.

00:34:40.920 --> 00:34:41.760
Just kidding!

00:34:46.690 --> 00:34:48.380
Hey!

00:34:49.950 --> 00:34:53.000
Must've been on a journey.

00:35:07.430 --> 00:35:08.790
Is everyone okay?

00:35:08.790 --> 00:35:09.520
Yeah.

00:35:09.520 --> 00:35:10.540
I'm fine.

00:35:10.540 --> 00:35:11.920
We're saved.

00:35:31.560 --> 00:35:32.670
Incredible!

00:35:32.670 --> 00:35:35.250
Fossils! The ammonite!

00:35:37.610 --> 00:35:37.910
All right! All right! I see them!

00:35:37.910 --> 00:35:40.610
Incredible!
All right! All right! I see them!

00:35:42.320 --> 00:35:45.280
See, I told you! They had to be in this cave.

00:35:45.550 --> 00:35:48.230
~Found it! Found it! Found it! Hoi!~

00:35:48.230 --> 00:35:50.580
~A mountain of fossils, found it! Hoi!~

00:35:51.280 --> 00:35:53.530
~Ammonite fossils! Hoi!~

00:35:53.530 --> 00:35:56.350
Ai! Hurry and come over here!

00:36:02.900 --> 00:36:03.930
Ai?

00:36:17.690 --> 00:36:18.660
Wonderful...

00:36:22.910 --> 00:36:24.480
What's that?

00:36:24.480 --> 00:36:26.710
A huge discovery.

00:36:26.710 --> 00:36:28.800
In-incredible!

00:36:28.800 --> 00:36:30.200
Earth-shaking.

00:36:30.490 --> 00:36:31.950
Earth-shaking?

00:36:31.950 --> 00:36:34.630
Earth-shaking is not the real name.

00:36:35.330 --> 00:36:39.550
I think it was... Sei-Seismosaurus!

00:36:39.900 --> 00:36:41.640
Seismosaurus?

00:36:41.640 --> 00:36:44.290
The world's largest animal!

00:36:44.290 --> 00:36:47.470
They say it can eat 500 kg in a day.

00:36:48.060 --> 00:36:49.890
The world's largest?!

00:36:50.430 --> 00:36:54.320
Ai, that's great! You know so much!

00:36:54.320 --> 00:36:57.390
No, I heard about it from Futo earlier.

00:36:57.840 --> 00:37:04.070
Futo says his dream is to one day complete the display at the museum.

00:37:04.070 --> 00:37:06.650
Well then, let's make that dream come true!

00:37:10.290 --> 00:37:11.880
Damn it!

00:37:16.280 --> 00:37:17.840
Yu, you all right?

00:37:17.840 --> 00:37:18.670
Damn.

00:37:19.300 --> 00:37:22.090
These rocks look like they are crumbling.

00:37:34.320 --> 00:37:36.230
Run for it!

00:37:37.020 --> 00:37:39.940
It really earned the name earth-shaking!

00:37:40.140 --> 00:37:41.610
Do you see an exit?

00:37:41.610 --> 00:37:43.530
We might be able to get out over there!

00:37:44.150 --> 00:37:45.990
You sea dogs, save yourselves!

00:37:45.990 --> 00:37:47.340
Oh!

00:37:56.660 --> 00:37:58.500
The Seismosaurus fossil!

00:37:59.090 --> 00:37:59.670
You can't!

00:38:00.010 --> 00:38:01.050
Let go!

00:38:01.050 --> 00:38:02.470
Give up, Yu!

00:38:02.470 --> 00:38:03.960
It's dangerous!

00:38:03.960 --> 00:38:05.430
Everyone is right!

00:38:25.240 --> 00:38:27.660
(Welcome!)

00:38:27.660 --> 00:38:29.950
(Play a game!)

00:38:29.950 --> 00:38:31.810
(Here we go!)

00:38:37.230 --> 00:38:41.000
Totakeke is still not appearing!

00:38:41.000 --> 00:38:44.350
Jeez, calm down a bit Bouquet.

00:38:47.330 --> 00:38:48.670
Sally, what's that?

00:38:53.190 --> 00:38:54.370
That's?

00:38:55.430 --> 00:38:58.770
I... can't seem to get the fossil's image out of my mind.

00:38:59.820 --> 00:39:03.020
I felt I had to transfer it onto a design.

00:39:03.020 --> 00:39:06.910
Once you have the image, no need for particulars.

00:39:07.260 --> 00:39:09.260
All that's left is to run with it.

00:39:11.120 --> 00:39:13.620
If I do that, no one can stop me.

00:39:14.420 --> 00:39:15.440
Sally.

00:39:17.360 --> 00:39:19.340
Hi! Such a splendid night.

00:39:19.340 --> 00:39:20.990
My name is Totakeke.

00:39:21.670 --> 00:39:23.610
Long ago I performed in front of the station,

00:39:23.610 --> 00:39:24.900
But now on Saturday nights,

00:39:25.260 --> 00:39:27.650
I perform live at the Pigeon's Roost.

00:39:28.320 --> 00:39:31.250
Thank you for coming to listen tonight.

00:39:32.080 --> 00:39:34.050
Are there any requests?

00:39:36.420 --> 00:39:37.980
K.K. Bossa please!

00:39:38.780 --> 00:39:39.450
OK!

00:40:26.990 --> 00:40:30.280
Once you have the image, no need for particulars.

00:40:30.990 --> 00:40:32.850
All that's left is to run with it.

00:40:35.320 --> 00:40:37.660
Becoming a designer is my dream!

00:40:38.400 --> 00:40:43.000
I hope, one day, people all over the world will be able to wear my clothes.

00:40:43.000 --> 00:40:45.620
I believe thinking about things is also a talent.

00:40:46.150 --> 00:40:47.960
Only because it would be a waste not to eat the food.

00:40:48.520 --> 00:40:51.790
You have to keep using them, or your talents may become rusty.

00:40:53.620 --> 00:40:54.760
This sketch book is...

00:40:58.580 --> 00:41:00.520
Sally's cherry pie, right?

00:41:32.080 --> 00:41:33.050
Thank you.

00:41:34.380 --> 00:41:35.960
Everyone, thank you.

00:42:04.140 --> 00:42:05.290
Look!

00:42:05.290 --> 00:42:06.940
See, you got it.

00:42:19.960 --> 00:42:22.770
Totakeke was the best!

00:42:24.100 --> 00:42:26.220
I felt a little embarrassed.

00:42:27.000 --> 00:42:32.750
K.K. Bossa. It was like he was singing out to me.

00:42:32.750 --> 00:42:35.380
I know it! I know it! That feeling!

00:42:35.380 --> 00:42:37.380
I want to taste it too.

00:42:38.990 --> 00:42:40.120
Not that.

00:42:41.240 --> 00:42:43.390
My very own cherry pie.

00:42:43.390 --> 00:42:44.160
What's that?

00:42:44.840 --> 00:42:45.840
Really?

00:42:48.400 --> 00:42:51.720
This is the golden sling shot! It's rare! rare!

00:42:51.720 --> 00:42:53.000
It's rare!

00:42:53.230 --> 00:42:55.940
My, my! Do you have a sharp eye!

00:42:55.940 --> 00:43:01.940
This item is one in a million. It gives you 100% accuracy they say.

00:43:01.940 --> 00:43:04.580
100% you say?!

00:43:05.120 --> 00:43:06.860
That's great!

00:43:07.740 --> 00:43:09.010
Hey!

00:43:09.010 --> 00:43:13.320
Don't you think those guys are getting a little carried away?

00:43:13.780 --> 00:43:16.480
Since today is the once a year fireworks festival,

00:43:16.480 --> 00:43:22.160
How about I give you a special price of 3,500 bells?

00:43:22.650 --> 00:43:25.750
This great slingshot for 3,500 bells?

00:43:25.750 --> 00:43:27.580
Real lucky!

00:43:27.940 --> 00:43:29.850
These boys...

00:43:29.850 --> 00:43:33.180
Hey! Ai! Sally! Bouquet!

00:43:33.810 --> 00:43:37.590
This shop is great! It's all hard to find items!

00:43:37.590 --> 00:43:39.820
Everyone come and look!

00:43:50.360 --> 00:43:52.050
Mayor.

00:43:55.110 --> 00:43:57.760
The name's Kotobuki!

00:44:03.420 --> 00:44:04.360
Mother.

00:44:04.950 --> 00:44:08.490
Today I was a little jealous of Sally.

00:44:09.160 --> 00:44:11.710
Being able to decide her own dream,

00:44:11.710 --> 00:44:13.990
living it out with conviction...

00:44:13.990 --> 00:44:15.670
...to the full extent.

00:44:23.860 --> 00:44:26.010
"Above the pine forest,

00:44:26.010 --> 00:44:28.860
on the night of the Winter festival, a miracle will occur."

00:44:30.840 --> 00:44:31.940
"Traveling to this star,

00:44:32.860 --> 00:44:37.570
I was unable to fulfill my wish."

00:44:37.570 --> 00:44:39.900
"Next, I'm coming to your planet."

00:44:41.630 --> 00:44:45.030
"Plant pine trees as marked on the map."

00:44:45.030 --> 00:44:47.750
"For the miracle to happen during the winter festival."

00:44:49.160 --> 00:44:53.940
"On the night of the winter festival, we can finally meet."

00:44:55.730 --> 00:44:57.050
Should I plant them?

00:44:57.720 --> 00:44:59.180
The pine trees.

00:45:03.690 --> 00:45:05.980
I still don't know what my dream is, but...

00:45:06.660 --> 00:45:07.580
Mother.

00:45:08.400 --> 00:45:11.980
However, I seem to be smelling its fragrance.

00:45:31.960 --> 00:45:34.790
Ai, why didn't you come!

00:45:35.090 --> 00:45:36.540
What do you mean?

00:45:36.540 --> 00:45:39.410
Sally's farewell party, of course!

00:45:39.410 --> 00:45:42.840
Sally looked really sad!

00:45:43.670 --> 00:45:45.730
If only Ai had come.

00:45:45.730 --> 00:45:47.860
Did Sally go somewhere?

00:45:48.690 --> 00:45:51.200
Don't tell me, you didn't hear?

00:45:51.200 --> 00:45:55.180
In order to become a designer, Sally is moving away.

00:45:57.440 --> 00:45:58.440
Ai!

00:46:31.870 --> 00:46:33.090
Sally.

00:46:39.690 --> 00:46:42.370
We'll be waiting for your next visit!

00:46:48.870 --> 00:46:52.450
Why is there a hole here!

00:46:55.480 --> 00:46:58.870
Now this looks splendid, eh, Sakura-jima?

00:46:58.870 --> 00:47:01.690
Stop laughing and help me out!

00:47:01.690 --> 00:47:07.500
A real man isn't so quick to ask for help from others.

00:47:07.500 --> 00:47:09.920
Your friend is in trouble here!

00:47:14.430 --> 00:47:17.100
Someone! Save me!

00:47:21.000 --> 00:47:22.000
We did it!

00:47:22.000 --> 00:47:23.330
A great success.

00:47:36.510 --> 00:47:39.300
This is nothing!

00:47:42.680 --> 00:47:45.670
I'm in top form today!

00:47:48.050 --> 00:47:50.990
Something this easy in one go!

00:48:01.790 --> 00:48:03.340
Was this a success?

00:48:04.040 --> 00:48:05.650
That was cool!

00:48:09.100 --> 00:48:09.920
It's Ai!

00:48:15.880 --> 00:48:17.350
All right!

00:48:19.520 --> 00:48:22.210
The secret hole plan is a success!

00:48:22.390 --> 00:48:24.960
All right! All right!

00:49:04.360 --> 00:49:06.150
At least it was big.

00:49:37.320 --> 00:49:38.940
Your usual blend?

00:50:12.930 --> 00:50:14.090
K.K. Bossa.

00:51:02.640 --> 00:51:06.080
The taste should be over the 80% mark.

00:51:06.940 --> 00:51:08.370
Please go ahead.

00:51:10.290 --> 00:51:11.490
Thank you.

00:51:24.900 --> 00:51:28.900
I am sure that Sally is listening to this same song right now.

00:51:55.000 --> 00:51:58.830
Oh my, why are you acting all depressed?

00:51:58.830 --> 00:52:00.570
Is it because your friend is moving?

00:52:01.720 --> 00:52:04.020
No matter what the circumstances,

00:52:04.020 --> 00:52:08.390
Being happy about your friends' decisions
is how to be a proper lady.

00:52:10.260 --> 00:52:13.940
There is no way I wouldn't be happy for Sally moving.

00:52:13.940 --> 00:52:14.880
Then what is it?

00:52:17.000 --> 00:52:18.790
She never said a word.

00:52:20.130 --> 00:52:22.570
She never said a word to me about moving.

00:52:23.410 --> 00:52:25.820
Master you heard?!

00:52:25.820 --> 00:52:28.330
Bianca, you also knew about it!

00:52:32.620 --> 00:52:33.290
I thought...

00:52:34.370 --> 00:52:36.390
...we were friends!

00:52:47.690 --> 00:52:49.540
Ah, silly.

00:52:50.500 --> 00:52:52.640
You're sillier than you look.

00:52:54.290 --> 00:52:59.210
If you thought you had a bond as a lady,
then you do without a doubt.

00:52:59.670 --> 00:53:01.870
Believe in yourself more.

00:53:01.870 --> 00:53:04.240
Believe in myself?

00:53:06.470 --> 00:53:10.500
If you believe in yourself, then your
friends will believe in you also.

00:53:13.200 --> 00:53:15.710
Think until you understand.

00:53:17.110 --> 00:53:19.310
It's Bianca's advice for the day.

00:53:21.150 --> 00:53:22.000
Okay.

00:53:25.440 --> 00:53:26.950
Thank you very much.

00:53:30.830 --> 00:53:31.880
What'll I do?

00:53:32.260 --> 00:53:34.890
Satisfy your coffee tab anytime you like.

00:53:35.440 --> 00:53:36.500
Thank you.

00:53:45.930 --> 00:53:48.050
A bond between women is lovely, yes?

00:53:49.750 --> 00:53:53.300
No matter how long or how far you are separated,

00:53:53.910 --> 00:53:58.150
The next time you meet it will be like it was just yesterday.

00:54:02.030 --> 00:54:04.970
However, a man and a woman are different.

00:54:06.970 --> 00:54:09.200
Even if it's just for one day,

00:54:09.640 --> 00:54:13.380
You can never return to how it was before.

00:54:23.380 --> 00:54:25.270
Excuse me.

00:54:26.600 --> 00:54:29.990
I'm real hu-hungry.

00:54:30.400 --> 00:54:33.920
I'm so hungry that I can't even move.

00:54:34.400 --> 00:54:37.070
I'm reaching the end.

00:54:37.070 --> 00:54:38.210
Are you okay?

00:54:38.680 --> 00:54:41.360
Do you have so-some food?

00:54:41.360 --> 00:54:43.430
My house is nearby.

00:54:43.430 --> 00:54:44.920
Can you make it that far?

00:54:45.190 --> 00:54:48.090
If you plan to give me some then...

00:55:02.230 --> 00:55:04.630
I'm sorry, this is all I had.

00:55:09.200 --> 00:55:11.390
Something caught in your throat?

00:55:12.350 --> 00:55:13.580
Here, some water.

00:55:18.290 --> 00:55:20.720
That really hit the spot.

00:55:28.250 --> 00:55:29.750
What is it?

00:55:30.290 --> 00:55:33.890
Seiichi is having so much fun eating, I was thinking.

00:55:34.430 --> 00:55:37.540
When you're starving, you become sad.

00:55:38.410 --> 00:55:41.900
And when you're sad, you become hungry.

00:55:42.920 --> 00:55:44.700
Have some.

00:55:54.890 --> 00:55:56.140
It's good.

00:56:04.240 --> 00:56:05.170
Yes!

00:56:09.700 --> 00:56:10.800
Miss Ai, right?

00:56:11.440 --> 00:56:12.530
A letter.

00:56:12.530 --> 00:56:13.430
Yes.

00:56:15.780 --> 00:56:16.600
Sally!

00:56:16.890 --> 00:56:17.900
Well then.

00:56:20.540 --> 00:56:21.810
Thank you very much!

00:56:22.840 --> 00:56:23.740
Seiichi!

00:56:46.160 --> 00:56:47.160
"Ai."

00:56:47.160 --> 00:56:48.170
"I'm sorry."

00:56:48.870 --> 00:56:52.030
"You're probably mad I kept it from you, right?"

00:56:53.730 --> 00:56:59.590
"But I knew, if I told you directly I would start to cry."

00:57:00.560 --> 00:57:01.800
"Even I would...

00:57:02.330 --> 00:57:03.440
...cry."

00:57:04.120 --> 00:57:08.790
"I didn't want to take the first step of my dream with tears in my eyes."

00:57:09.680 --> 00:57:14.640
"I knew my friend Ai who always supported me would understand."

00:57:22.440 --> 00:57:25.470
"Please forgive my selfishness."

00:57:26.480 --> 00:57:28.560
"Your best friend in the whole world..."

00:57:28.970 --> 00:57:29.750
"Sally."

00:57:41.270 --> 00:57:44.100
(The color white is an outline for your spoon)

00:57:47.750 --> 00:57:51.480
Now it's your turn to eat your very own cherry pie.

00:57:56.460 --> 00:58:02.200
Sally has been helping me prepare for the next step.

00:58:03.740 --> 00:58:04.630
This time.

00:58:05.250 --> 00:58:06.340
It's my turn.

00:58:12.120 --> 00:58:15.520
I'll also try hard!

00:58:15.520 --> 00:58:17.450
Ai, what's wrong?

00:58:19.380 --> 00:58:21.980
Suddenly yelling is surprising.

00:58:22.570 --> 00:58:24.450
Bouquet, what is it?

00:58:25.510 --> 00:58:26.310
Earler today...

00:58:27.580 --> 00:58:30.580
I said some harsh things.

00:58:30.580 --> 00:58:32.730
No way, is that it?

00:58:32.730 --> 00:58:37.070
No way? You were really downcast.

00:58:39.490 --> 00:58:42.830
I just received a letter from Sally.

00:58:42.830 --> 00:58:44.160
Can I see it too?

00:58:44.500 --> 00:58:45.250
Of course!

00:58:47.830 --> 00:58:49.610
A shooting star!

00:58:55.620 --> 00:58:56.650
Another!

00:58:59.090 --> 00:59:01.310
A meteor shower!

00:59:14.840 --> 00:59:18.340
I hope that Sally's transition goes real well.

00:59:21.640 --> 00:59:22.560
Mother.

00:59:23.120 --> 00:59:26.720
Sally believed in herself and left the village.

00:59:28.070 --> 00:59:30.990
Next is my turn, she said in a letter.

00:59:33.880 --> 00:59:37.520
Sally and Bouquet have always believed in me.

00:59:38.180 --> 00:59:43.230
I think I'll try to believe in myself a little more too.

00:59:46.800 --> 00:59:47.590
P.S-

00:59:48.710 --> 00:59:52.800
Mother, it seems people become sad when they are hungry.

00:59:53.720 --> 00:59:56.380
Please keep your stomach full always.

01:00:16.520 --> 01:00:18.190
Ai!

01:00:20.790 --> 01:00:22.340
Bouquet!

01:00:22.340 --> 01:00:25.100
How is my cute set up?

01:00:25.290 --> 01:00:28.640
With this, I'll definitely be this year's winner!

01:00:28.970 --> 01:00:31.320
It has that Bouquet feel, nice!

01:00:32.110 --> 01:00:33.710
Thank you!

01:00:33.710 --> 01:00:36.420
Ai, have fun at the festival!

01:00:36.420 --> 01:00:41.070
I don't know about stars or aliens, but don't study all day!

01:00:41.560 --> 01:00:44.990
It's okay, it's okay! I'll be eating my cherry pie for sure!

01:00:45.680 --> 01:00:47.220
More cherry pies?

01:00:58.880 --> 01:01:02.180
There sure are a lot of pine trees this year.

01:01:02.580 --> 01:01:05.600
Who could have planted all of them?

01:01:07.650 --> 01:01:14.560
Since we have to decorate all the trees that have been planted then...

01:01:16.580 --> 01:01:19.990
Taking down all the lights is my problem?!

01:01:21.040 --> 01:01:23.380
Everyone in the Animal village.

01:01:23.380 --> 01:01:26.310
The commencement of the winter festival is starting.

01:01:26.310 --> 01:01:31.850
Whomever has the best decorations will be this year's winner!

01:01:33.030 --> 01:01:39.820
Also, the electoral proceedings for the mayor have started, don't forget to vote.

01:01:40.900 --> 01:01:45.260
Blatant advertising is definitely against the rules, jeez.

01:01:46.240 --> 01:01:48.820
Let's close our eyes, Sis.

01:01:49.320 --> 01:01:51.180
The mayor is desperate.

01:01:51.450 --> 01:01:54.100
Way too busy! Way too busy!

01:02:03.690 --> 01:02:05.450
What was that now?

01:02:19.420 --> 01:02:21.090
No way. I'm getting old.

01:02:26.500 --> 01:02:27.650
This tree.

01:02:29.530 --> 01:02:31.910
Has gotten really big.

01:02:43.030 --> 01:02:45.180
I wonder if it will really happen.

01:02:45.180 --> 01:02:48.120
This year's winter festival miracle.

01:03:08.030 --> 01:03:10.470
Sis, come take a look.

01:03:42.370 --> 01:03:43.630
Fuko!

01:03:44.290 --> 01:03:47.260
The new snow is slippery, so take care!

01:03:47.260 --> 01:03:51.680
The Animal village, the Animal village festivities have started!

01:03:52.890 --> 01:03:56.600
Tonight, all the hidden stars in the sky will come out to play!

01:03:59.080 --> 01:04:04.940
Even during this cold winter, I can understand their warm-hearted feelings too.

01:04:07.950 --> 01:04:09.360
Pretty!

01:04:10.750 --> 01:04:12.780
Were you able to see something?

01:04:12.780 --> 01:04:14.300
Nothing at all.

01:04:22.360 --> 01:04:23.540
What's wrong?

01:04:23.840 --> 01:04:26.010
Lately, I've been thinking.

01:04:26.730 --> 01:04:31.300
The message bottles might just be a prank.

01:04:31.630 --> 01:04:35.130
And I thought it was sent by UFO's without reason.

01:04:38.190 --> 01:04:40.000
On the night of the winter festival,

01:04:40.000 --> 01:04:42.020
a visitor flying on a UFO,

01:04:42.020 --> 01:04:44.050
will come to Animal Village.

01:04:44.770 --> 01:04:46.770
A fantastic speculation.

01:04:47.010 --> 01:04:49.660
But it's not something most people would come up with.

01:04:49.660 --> 01:04:51.650
It's not really that far-fetched.

01:04:53.390 --> 01:04:56.580
The idea of UFOs is a common topic.

01:04:56.580 --> 01:05:00.100
The idea of it just being cult-fiction has passed.

01:05:00.100 --> 01:05:03.460
The reality exists, but nothing has been confirmed.

01:05:03.850 --> 01:05:05.880
So the chances are not null.

01:05:06.570 --> 01:05:10.260
When you're the one saying it, I get excited again.

01:05:11.170 --> 01:05:12.540
Keep the feeling!

01:05:12.540 --> 01:05:15.970
At least until the festival is over lets keep an eye out.

01:05:16.520 --> 01:05:20.040
I want to meet them, people from another planet!

01:05:20.040 --> 01:05:20.750
Yeah!

01:05:24.170 --> 01:05:24.980
What's wrong?

01:05:25.920 --> 01:05:26.990
UFO!

01:05:29.950 --> 01:05:31.170
It's bad!

01:05:55.590 --> 01:05:57.510
Red Alert!

01:05:57.510 --> 01:06:00.180
A UFO has crashed!

01:06:01.450 --> 01:06:02.750
UFO he said?

01:06:02.750 --> 01:06:04.020
UFO?

01:06:04.730 --> 01:06:06.310
What? A UFO?

01:06:07.810 --> 01:06:10.110
It fell in that part of the forest!

01:06:39.270 --> 01:06:40.480
Here, here!

01:06:40.480 --> 01:06:43.440
Incredible! It's a real UFO.

01:06:47.310 --> 01:06:48.850
Futo, hold on!

01:06:49.740 --> 01:06:51.150
I'm getting chills.

01:06:55.290 --> 01:06:57.460
They really exist, right, Ai?

01:06:57.460 --> 01:06:58.240
Yeah.

01:06:58.820 --> 01:07:00.310
Was there an alien inside?

01:07:01.260 --> 01:07:05.810
Be careful! If you get too close you'll be hit by an alien laser beam!

01:07:06.210 --> 01:07:08.210
Or they may put a chip in your brain!

01:07:09.090 --> 01:07:10.710
You boys again.

01:07:33.960 --> 01:07:37.670
Hello Earth! And Earth people, pleased to meet...

01:07:56.240 --> 01:07:57.300
You okay?

01:07:58.160 --> 01:07:59.510
Of course!

01:08:01.850 --> 01:08:03.050
That was painful.

01:08:05.090 --> 01:08:06.220
Pleased to meet you!

01:08:07.360 --> 01:08:09.200
Are you an alien?

01:08:10.160 --> 01:08:11.860
Yes!

01:08:12.560 --> 01:08:16.580
Hello Earth! And Earth people, pleased to meet you.

01:08:16.580 --> 01:08:18.350
You're a big liar!

01:08:20.360 --> 01:08:25.000
Actually, something bumped into me up above.

01:08:25.000 --> 01:08:28.040
Everyone, I have a request.

01:08:28.040 --> 01:08:31.290
Can you please help me look for the UFO components?

01:08:31.290 --> 01:08:32.390
UFO components?

01:08:32.390 --> 01:08:36.910
When I was hit there were five parts that went flying.

01:08:37.300 --> 01:08:40.020
I still haven't paid off my bank loan.

01:08:40.020 --> 01:08:40.840
Loan?

01:08:42.610 --> 01:08:46.030
Without those parts, I can't return to space!

01:08:46.030 --> 01:08:48.840
If I can't go home, my life will meet it's...

01:08:50.730 --> 01:08:52.190
Oh, no!

01:08:53.400 --> 01:08:54.670
What should we do?

01:08:55.620 --> 01:08:57.270
This guy is real suspicious.

01:08:57.270 --> 01:09:00.010
Sis, that's rude to say out loud.

01:09:00.400 --> 01:09:03.120
So, to sum it all up,

01:09:03.510 --> 01:09:06.910
unless we find your parts you can't go home, right?

01:09:07.290 --> 01:09:08.840
Now that you mention it.

01:09:08.840 --> 01:09:12.490
A moment ago I saw a shooting star falling in the area.

01:09:15.900 --> 01:09:17.180
Then, we should...

01:09:17.180 --> 01:09:19.320
Search the mountains for the UFO.

01:09:19.320 --> 01:09:19.860
Right.

01:09:19.860 --> 01:09:22.030
I'll head towards the ocean.

01:09:22.670 --> 01:09:25.060
Brother, let's look this way.

01:09:26.860 --> 01:09:28.050
What is it, Yu!?

01:09:28.050 --> 01:09:28.950
It had to be!

01:09:28.950 --> 01:09:30.850
Yu, wait up!

01:09:31.070 --> 01:09:33.040
Had to be, what?

01:09:33.040 --> 01:09:34.770
I'm coming too!

01:09:35.240 --> 01:09:36.610
Earlier, I saw it.

01:09:36.610 --> 01:09:38.970
Something sparkling in the sky.

01:09:38.970 --> 01:09:44.610
It couldn't have been flying. It must've been a falling UFO part.

01:09:53.010 --> 01:09:55.420
Did it really fall in the cave?

01:09:55.420 --> 01:09:56.660
Probably.

01:09:56.660 --> 01:09:57.880
I'm done for it.

01:09:58.410 --> 01:09:59.750
It's useless.

01:09:59.750 --> 01:10:00.800
Useless.

01:10:00.800 --> 01:10:03.230
Don't give up so easily!

01:10:13.720 --> 01:10:14.520
Sally?

01:10:15.570 --> 01:10:20.440
Sally!

01:10:20.640 --> 01:10:24.620
I had the holiday off, so I came to join the festival.

01:10:24.990 --> 01:10:27.350
Everyone was talking about the UFO.

01:10:27.350 --> 01:10:30.870
And they said I could find Ai if I looked in this area.

01:10:31.880 --> 01:10:34.790
Sally, thank you for the letter.

01:10:37.510 --> 01:10:39.430
You came back just in time, Sally.

01:10:39.430 --> 01:10:40.550
You saved us.

01:10:40.550 --> 01:10:42.430
Now, leave the rest to me!

01:10:45.560 --> 01:10:48.550
Wait up! Don't head off alone!

01:10:48.550 --> 01:10:50.680
Wait up!

01:11:16.560 --> 01:11:17.450
Over there!

01:11:18.980 --> 01:11:20.250
Where, where?

01:11:20.690 --> 01:11:21.990
The fossil!

01:11:23.660 --> 01:11:25.360
On top of the dinosaur fossil!

01:11:29.530 --> 01:11:31.110
That's dangerous, Yu!

01:11:31.110 --> 01:11:33.760
Have you forgotten? The rock will start crumbling!

01:11:38.300 --> 01:11:41.770
That was in the summer. But now, the cold weather has hardened it.

01:11:41.770 --> 01:11:44.000
I can climb it, I must climb it!

01:11:44.000 --> 01:11:45.940
That alien's life is at stake!

01:12:07.970 --> 01:12:09.070
Yu!

01:12:09.410 --> 01:12:10.220
Incredible.

01:12:37.350 --> 01:12:41.070
Way high! You guys look like little ants!

01:12:41.070 --> 01:12:44.370
Forget about that! Make sure you don't fall!

01:12:44.370 --> 01:12:45.570
I'm fine!

01:12:49.260 --> 01:12:50.490
Over there.

01:13:15.960 --> 01:13:16.740
Just a bit more.

01:13:33.240 --> 01:13:34.730
I did it!

01:13:35.500 --> 01:13:36.850
All right!

01:13:48.520 --> 01:13:49.190
Where's the part?

01:13:49.770 --> 01:13:51.610
I can't see ahead.

01:14:05.370 --> 01:14:07.170
Yu!

01:14:07.360 --> 01:14:10.800
We'll catch you, don't worry!

01:14:11.450 --> 01:14:13.000
I'm too scared!

01:14:19.810 --> 01:14:20.870
I won't make it!

01:14:20.870 --> 01:14:21.720
Ai!

01:14:42.390 --> 01:14:43.760
Help me!

01:14:45.210 --> 01:14:47.750
I'm not a good swimmer.

01:14:52.070 --> 01:14:53.530
I'm sorry.

01:14:59.070 --> 01:15:00.390
Nice catch, Ai.

01:15:10.480 --> 01:15:11.410
What is it?

01:15:12.000 --> 01:15:15.110
This is the first time I've seen your real face.

01:15:17.760 --> 01:15:18.940
One.

01:15:18.940 --> 01:15:20.190
Two.

01:15:20.190 --> 01:15:21.430
Three.

01:15:21.430 --> 01:15:22.530
Four.

01:15:22.530 --> 01:15:24.660
And, one more.

01:15:25.860 --> 01:15:26.870
We found it!

01:15:26.870 --> 01:15:27.600
Found it!
We found it!

01:15:27.600 --> 01:15:28.460
Found it!

01:15:37.240 --> 01:15:37.990
Here.

01:15:37.990 --> 01:15:38.910
What?!

01:15:38.910 --> 01:15:41.670
Oh, no! Why are there two?!

01:15:42.010 --> 01:15:43.160
It's true!

01:15:43.160 --> 01:15:44.660
What does it mean?

01:16:16.350 --> 01:16:18.330
The miracle of the winter festival.

01:16:33.780 --> 01:16:35.120
This part is alive.

01:16:35.120 --> 01:16:36.420
